      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a fair point about subconscious bias, but let's look at it from the perspective of a prosecutor or a defense attorney trying to win. If an attorney wanted to cast doubt on Transcript B, they might argue that the informal grammar and \"slang\" suggest a lack of attention to detail or a less disciplined mind. Do you think there's any truth to the idea that a more standard, \"proper\" way of speaking correlates with better observation skills or a more logical way of processing an event?",
