      "content": "An attorney can certainly use perceived informality to suggest poor attention to detail, but this is an argument about character, not necessarily the facts of the event itself. There is no inherent correlation proving that \"proper\" grammar equates to superior observation skills; people of all educational backgrounds can be highly observant. However, in the high-stakes environment of a courtroom, attorneys often leverage stylistic weaknesses to plant seeds of doubt, even if those seeds lack substantial factual support.",
